--  The run-time checks of the library build (ADASMB_CONTRACT_CHECKS=proved, the
--  default), as docs/platinum-design.md decides: preconditions, which guard
--  the core against its trusted callers, and the assertions in the code stay
--  checked; postconditions are not run, because GNATprove proves them and the
--  specifications they use are costly to run (one such as "the digest is
--  SHA-256 of the message" would compute the hash again on every call). Ghost
--  code stays (Check) because some preconditions call ghost functions; it
--  runs only where a precondition, an assertion or a ghost statement uses it.
--  -XADASMB_CONTRACT_CHECKS=all, and the test build, check everything but
--  the contracts the source itself marks as never run, whose specifications
--  recurse: over the whole input, as Core_Text.UTF8_To_UTF16's postcondition
--  does, or over a block's rounds, as the Crypto body's from SHA256_Compress
--  on do (the stack check rejects recursion reachable from SMB.Client).
--
--  It applies to every source of smb.gpr, including the trusted units that
--  GNATprove does not prove (SMB.Client, SMB.Transport, the platform units);
--  tests/check_sources.py keeps postconditions out of those.
pragma Assertion_Policy
  (Pre => Check,
   Pre'Class => Check,
   Post => Ignore,
   Post'Class => Ignore,
   Refined_Post => Ignore,
   Contract_Cases => Ignore,
   Assert => Check,
   Assert_And_Cut => Check,
   Assume => Check,
   Loop_Invariant => Check,
   Loop_Variant => Check,
   Ghost => Check);
